MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The compact duct tape and super glue fit the small repair tasks suggested by my screws and anchors: they offer practical ways to secure things when fasteners are inconvenient.",
    "Both tape rolls felt relevant as general repair supplies, though I would choose the compact roll now because I do not need two rolls for the same purpose."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The backer rod, diamond burrs, and air filtration system require specific sealing, grinding, or workshop needs that my fastener purchases do not establish.",
    "Replacement vacuum bags suggest maintaining an existing vacuum, not needing a carpet cleaner or pet formula. The audio converter, water tester, and infrared thermometer also lack a connection to a task I currently have."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My construction fasteners seem to have been taken as evidence that I want a broad range of workshop equipment, although my recent choices mainly concern fastening and mounting.",
    "My household maintenance purchases seem to have been stretched into interest in unrelated cleaning products and measuring devices."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The useful connection is whether an item helps with my current repair tasks; being another tool or household supply is not enough.",
    "My vacuum bags are explicitly made for particular Panasonic types, so compatibility matters for replacement supplies. That purchase gives little reason to assume I need a different cleaning system."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my practical repair needs but assumed too many additional projects and equipment needs from a few specific purchases."
}
